To say 'on [day of the week]', is the same as just the day so 'gievgia' can mean 'thursday' and 'on thursday'. 

To say 'on [day of the week]s', put 'il' or 'la' depending on the gender before the day of the week. Depsipte the fact that it is plural, you still use the singular in this case, so 'la gievgia' --> 'On thursdays' and 'Il venderdi' --> 'On fridays' 

For days of the week, the gender is pretty easy: If it ends with 'a', it's femenine, else it's masculine